<title>BELGIUM: EU beef market returning to normal - Commission.</title>
<headline>EU beef market returning to normal - Commission.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bids to sell beef into intervention have fallen to 18,000 tonnes this week showing that European Union markets are returning to normal, a European Commission official said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Beef intervention buying is not likely to be much more than 7,000 tonnes at today's beef management committee meeting,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The beef market has been hit since March by fears for the product's safety due to a scare of mad cow disease.</p>
<p>The official said falling intervention price and seasonal difficulties are factors contributing to the drop in intervention demand but the Commission is confident that markets have returned almost to normal.</p>
<p>The Commission has been prepared to buy-in up to 25,000 tonnes of beef at each of the twice monthly EU beef management committee meetings.</p>
<p>Intervention purchases usually represent about half the total offers.</p>
</text>
